  "body": "What happens: `assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps` line 157 decides inch/mm from the machine file:\n\n    inch = typeof machine !== \"undefined\" && machine.units === \"inch\";\n\nSince #902 the posted unit comes from the document only (`postOptions.Units`), never the machine file. A sinker program for an inch document on a machine file that says mm (or the reverse) would be posted in the wrong unit.\n\nExpected: the post reads the document's unit, as `assets/posts/wire-iso.cps` line 137 does (`postOptions.Units === \"inch\"`), and declares `programUnits` the same way if it supports both.\n\nEvidence: batch gate 11 on main `dda168480` is red in one test (8 of 9 steps green):\n`camcraft-app`, binary `program_units`, test `no_shipped_post_takes_the_program_unit_from_the_machine_file`:\n\n    panicked at crates\\app\\tests\\program_units.rs:228:9:\n    ...assets/posts\\sinker-iso.cps: reads machine.units\n\nStill present on `origin/main` at `8d4e54db`. Came in with PR #1141 (sinker ISO post), which merged after the program-units law (PR #981) reached main; neither PR's own gate saw the other.\n\nDone means: `sinker-iso.cps` takes the unit from the document; `program_units` is green; a test pins that a sinker program posts in the document's unit when the machine file says the other one (or the post refuses by name what it cannot write); the sinker goldens still hold.\n",
